
### 1. Get all heroes — expect 200
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/heroes/

### 2. Create Spider-Man — expect 200
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/heroes/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Spider-Man",
  "age": 25,
  "secret_name": "Peter Parker"
}

### 3. Create Batman — expect 200
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/heroes/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Batman",
  "age": 35,
  "secret_name": "Bruce Wayne"
}

### 4. Get one hero using pagination — expect 200
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/heroes/?limit=1

### 5. Skip the first hero — expect 200
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/heroes/?offset=1

### 6. Get Spider-Man by ID — expect 200
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/heroes/1

### 7. Update Spider-Man — expect 200
PATCH http://127.0.0.1:8000/heroes/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Updated Hero",
  "age": 30
}

### 8. Delete Spider-Man — expect 200
DELETE http://127.0.0.1:8000/heroes/1

### 9. Get a non-existent hero — expect 404
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/heroes/999

### 10. Update a non-existent hero — expect 404
PATCH http://127.0.0.1:8000/heroes/999
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ghost Hero"
}

### 11. Verify deleted hero is gone — expect 404
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/heroes/1

### 12. Delete a non-existent hero — expect 404
DELETE http://127.0.0.1:8000/heroes/999
